{#- The Cite buttons' data, followed by the behavior that consumes it.

    The map used to be hand-maintained at the top of static/js/citation.js, one
    BibTeX entry per paper, duplicating content/citations.bib, which duplicated
    content/publications.yml. Three copies, and the site shipped the one nobody
    was checking: the ICE paper's Cite button opened an empty modal for months
    because its key was on the page and in neither bibliography.

    The behavior half is still a real, lintable .js file under static/ --
    appended here rather than templated, since none of it depends on content. #}
/* Generated by build.py from content/publications.yml and content/software.yml.
   Edits here are discarded on the next build -- see sitegen/bibtex.py. */
window.CITATIONS = {
{% for key, entry in citations.items() %}
    '{{ key }}': `{{ entry }}`{{ "," if not loop.last }}
{% endfor %}
};

{{ inline('js/citation-modal.js') }}
